WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:05.279
The seasons are always changing, but Game
of Thrones fans know that everything is just

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.380
one Long Winter until the final season of
the series arrives in 2019.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.040
Until the show returns to the air, though,
all we can really do is speculate.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.180
Here are all the rumors about Game of Thrones'
final season.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.460
A bloody end for Arya

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.680
Maisie Williams, who plays Arya, posted a
picture to her Instagram of her sneakers covered

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.420
in blood, on her last day of shooting.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.520
That seems to imply that her final scene will
involve some seriously bloody combat.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.070
But will Arya survive?

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.340
"What do we say to the god of death?"

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:36.480
"Not today."

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.980
Either way, she says the final filming for
her character took place in Belfast, where

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.300
the scenes in Winterfell and the North are
shot.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.820
Based on this geotag clue alone, it seems
like however her bloody story ends, it'll

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.460
be in the North.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.960
Brother from another mother

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:57.380
Lena Headey also dropped a sneaky reference
to season 8 on her own Instagram after snapping

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:03.399
a pic with her onscreen brothers Peter Dinklage
and Nikolaj Coster-Waldau captioned, "Congratulations

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.760
to my brothers (literally) from other mothers.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.500
I'm a lucky lucky sista to these Mistas."

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.500
Is Headey insinuating that Tyrion's parentage
is a bit more complicated than it seems?

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.980
Multiple sources, including the Independent,
have speculated that Tyrion is actually the

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.600
bastard son of Joanna Lannister and Aerys
Targaryen - making him Daenerys' half-brother.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:27.600
Of course, Headey uses the word "mothers,"
not father, so maybe Headey is just making

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.760
a cute Instagram post.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.120
Sansa in charge

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.310
When we first catch up with Sansa in season
8, she's going to be ruling the roost at Winterfell

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.360
while Jon is away.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.140
However, in an interview with Digital Spy,
actress Sophie Turner mentioned that she wrapped

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.160
shooting in Spain.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.460
That's where Dragonstone and the Dragonpit
are filmed, which means that although Sansa

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.149
might be running Winterfell at the start of
the season, she's going to wind up heading

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:52.140
south at some point.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.700
In addition, Watchers on the Wall reports
that filming at the Roman ruins of Itálica

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:01.889
in Spain a.k.a. the Dragonpit were scheduled
for over four weeks, hinting that the location

00:02:01.889 --> 00:02:04.240
will be of far greater importance in season
8.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:09.220
This news feeds into the abundance of rumors
that Sansa is going to come away the ultimate

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.520
winner of the Game of Thrones.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:17.640
"Now I'm sure cutting off heads is very satisfying,
but that's not the way you get people to work

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:18.140
together."

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.260
Some fans have even theorized that she might
wind up marrying Gendry and become the Queen

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.240
of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.820
Give these boys a hand

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:33.380
In an interview with WRadio at Bogota Comic-Con,
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau revealed that Jaime

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.640
will be interacting with Liam Cunningham's
Davos for the first time this season.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.430
Since Davos is currently serving as Jon Snow's
hand, the news of their impending interactions

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:46.890
confirms the theory that Jaime is going to
make it all the way North to team up with

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:47.960
Jon and Daenerys.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.920
Return of the bear queen

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.540
Played by Bella Ramsey, Lyanna Mormont was
instrumental in installing Jon Snow as King

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.430
in the North in season 6.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.440
"Ned Stark's blood runs through his veins.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.980
He's my king, from this day until his last
day."

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:09.520
According to the Watchers on the Wall, Ramsey
was spotted on set in Belfast, implying that

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.510
she's still involved in the game.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:15.340
However, will she be withdrawing her support
once she learns that her King has bent the

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.680
knee to a foreign queen?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.100
Biggest battle ever

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:24.580
In a now-deleted Instagram post, assistant
director Jonathan Quinlan captioned a thank-you

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.670
note to the crew: "55 consecutive nights.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:28.819
11 weeks.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:29.600
3 locations.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.240
You'll never again see anything like it."

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:36.420
Quinlan's thank-you note mentioned that the
crew had been working tirelessly in Northern

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:36.920
Ireland.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.400
Based on the show's previous filming locations,
it's safe to assume that this record-breaking

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.340
massive battle will take place in the North,
and it's likely to be the final battle against

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.280
the Night King.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.500
Ending at King's Landing

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:54.019
Rumors from The Dubrovnik Times indicate that
the last scene of the entire series may very

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.800
well take place at King's Landing.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.599
Nothing is official, of course, but wouldn't
the home of the Iron Throne be a fitting location

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.680
to end the series all about the fight for
said seat of power?

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:05.360
The missing Mountain

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:12.420
Interviewed in January 2018, Hafþór Júlíus
Björnsson who plays Ser Gregor "the Mountain"

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.700
Clegane, wasn't all that forthcoming about
his involvement in season 8.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.520
This led fans to speculate over whether this
meant Björnsson wouldn't be on set for long.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:24.290
Will the Mountain finally fall to The Hound
in the long-awaited battle fans have been

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.280
clamoring for?

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.500
Or maybe Arya will finally manage to cross
his name off her list?

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.340
Plenty of death

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.640
Get ready to say goodbye to at least some
of your favorites.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:39.160
In an interview with the Hollywood Reporter,
HBO senior VP Francesca Orsi explained that

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:43.450
the final moments of Game of Thrones are going
to spell doom for multiple characters.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.980
Talking about the final table read with the
entire cast, she said,

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:51.290
"None of the cast had received the scripts
prior, and one by one they started to fall

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.630
down to their deaths.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:57.040
By the end, the last few words on the final
script, the tears just started falling down."

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.940
"When you play the game of thrones, you win
or you die.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:03.600
There is no middle ground."

